ground oil tobacco product. It comes in loose or in pouches. Larger pouches, one

452
00:33:39,581 --> 00:33:44,340
gram size, they're smaller pouches. You use it between the upper lip and gum and

453
00:33:44,341 --> 00:33:48,580
it comes in various flavors. Swedish snus is the most discreet of smokeless

454
00:33:48,581 --> 00:33:49,281
products.

455
00:33:49,282 --> 00:33:53,840
Besides being barely visible, it doesn't involve spitting and is used by half

456
00:33:53,841 --> 00:33:58,580
of Swedish tobacco consumers who absorb doses of nicotine from Snus through their mouths.

457
00:34:00,280 --> 00:34:04,660
As with all forms of smokeless tobacco, users show increased incidence of oral cancer over

458
00:34:04,661 --> 00:34:05,516
non-users.

459
00:34:05,517 --> 00:34:11,940
Swedish Snus is the mainstay of Swedish Match, a nearly century-old Swedish

460
00:34:11,941 --> 00:34:15,776
company that markets both premium and machine-made cigars.

461
00:34:15,777 --> 00:34:17,760
Chewing tobacco, pipe tobacco,

462
00:34:17,761 --> 00:34:22,760
Moist snuff, matches, lighters, and snus.

463
00:34:24,760 --> 00:34:28,760
What separates Americans from their Swedish smokeless counterparts is spitting.

464
00:34:28,761 --> 00:34:31,760
American favorites, moist snuff and chewing tobacco,

465
00:34:31,761 --> 00:34:35,760
are placed between the lower lip and gong, requiring expectoration,

466
00:34:35,761 --> 00:34:38,760
and are primarily used in rural areas.

467
00:34:39,760 --> 00:34:42,760
Moist snuff is a ground tobacco product,

468
00:34:42,761 --> 00:34:45,760
but chewing tobacco comes as a cut leaf.

469
00:34:45,761 --> 00:34:50,260
Chewing tobacco is cut and stripped to a certain size.

470
00:34:50,780 --> 00:34:56,360
It is then processed and then we put what is called a casing that's essentially a top flavoring on the product.

471
00:34:57,060 --> 00:35:00,120
It's usually a molasses or a sugar type flavoring on the product.

472
00:35:00,320 --> 00:35:03,920
It is then dried to a specified point and then is put into a pouch.

473
00:35:05,140 --> 00:35:07,680
Swedish Match's chewing tobacco is called Redman.

474
00:35:08,880 --> 00:35:13,640
It was originally produced by the Pinkerton Tobacco Company in Ohio starting in 1904.

475
00:35:13,641 --> 00:35:18,640
To this day, it's still the most popular form of chewing tobacco that's on the market.

476
00:35:18,641 --> 00:35:24,640
But no matter what your preference, if you're a tobacco user, there are almost as many quitting products as tobacco products.

477
00:35:24,641 --> 00:35:28,640
And much like consuming, how you quit is a matter of taste.

478
00:35:28,641 --> 00:35:35,640
Chewing or snuffing tobacco ten times a day can deliver the same amount of nicotine to the body as smoking 30 to 40 cigarettes.

479
00:35:35,641 --> 00:35:42,640
Of all the people who smoke cigarettes, for example, 70 to 80 percent or more are addicted.

480
00:35:42,641 --> 00:35:49,280
If you look at alcohol use, probably 5 or 10% of all alcohol users are addicted.

481
00:35:49,860 --> 00:35:53,360
And even if you look at cocaine and heroin, there's a lot of casual use,

482
00:35:53,440 --> 00:35:58,080
and probably 50% or fewer cocaine and heroin users are actually addicted.

483
00:35:58,800 --> 00:36:04,160
So by those criteria, nicotine is the most addictive of the various addictive substances people use.

484
00:36:05,040 --> 00:36:09,520
Once it enters the brain, nicotine causes the release of a cascade of hormones.

485
00:36:10,280 --> 00:36:12,620
Dopamine, serotonin, and endorphins.

486
00:36:12,640 --> 00:36:16,120
which increase pleasure, reduce appetite, and improve mood.

487
00:36:17,440 --> 00:36:20,760
But nicotine also alters the chemical structure of a smoker's brain.

488
00:36:22,200 --> 00:36:27,920
The brain will produce more nicotine receptors that then need to get activated.

489
00:36:28,180 --> 00:36:31,580
So then the brain is going to want to seek more nicotine,

490
00:36:31,680 --> 00:36:33,760
and a person is going to do that by smoking.

491
00:36:34,800 --> 00:36:39,000
Without cigarettes, smokers may experience withdrawal symptoms in as little an hour.

492
00:36:40,060 --> 00:36:41,660
Withdrawal symptoms are terrible.

493
00:36:41,661 --> 00:36:43,835
People feel really rotten.

494
00:36:43,836 --> 00:36:49,440
They feel irritable, angry, they have insomnia, can feel depressed.

495
00:36:50,380 --> 00:36:54,920
For smokers who attempt to quit, there are a number of approaches to overcoming withdrawal symptoms.

496
00:36:55,560 --> 00:36:59,160
Some people respond better to behavioral therapy, some to pharmacotherapy,

497
00:36:59,500 --> 00:37:01,800
some a combination of behavioral and pharmacotherapy,

498
00:37:02,100 --> 00:37:05,240
and then there are those few who go cold turkey and just say, I'm going to do it.

499
00:37:05,480 --> 00:37:07,280
Not real common, but they do it.

500
00:37:08,280 --> 00:37:10,820
More succeed by developing a plan with a counselor.

501
00:37:11,660 --> 00:37:18,220
The idea with getting the counseling and the professional support is, okay, what am I going to do in that situation?

502
00:37:18,680 --> 00:37:22,960
When I feel stressed, what can I do instead of grabbing for a cigarette?

503
00:37:23,540 --> 00:37:26,420
On the technological side, there are three types of quitting medications.

504
00:37:26,900 --> 00:37:28,760
Some require a prescription and some don't.

505
00:37:29,200 --> 00:37:38,120
The first category is nicotine replacement therapy in the form of gum, inhaler, nasal spray, patch, or lozenge.

506
00:37:38,121 --> 00:37:44,760
nicotine replacement provides less than half the nicotine a smoker would normally get

507
00:37:44,761 --> 00:37:51,840
and tapers off over the 12-week course of treatment the second category is bupropion

508
00:37:51,841 --> 00:38:00,140
which is also known as zyban which was marketed originally and still is as an antidepressant

509
00:38:00,141 --> 00:38:06,660
but it was found that people taking this drug had less craving for cigarettes and it turns out that

510
00:38:06,661 --> 00:38:13,700
The effects of bupropion resemble effects of nicotine in the pattern of hormone release in the brain.

511
00:38:14,440 --> 00:38:16,640
A third category is a drug, berenicline.

512
00:38:17,140 --> 00:38:23,960
This is a totally new category of drug, which has got nicotine-like effects, but also nicotine-blocking effects.

513
00:38:24,460 --> 00:38:30,840
The nicotine-blocking effects mean that if you have a lapse or a slip and you smoke a cigarette, it's not as satisfying.

514
00:38:31,120 --> 00:38:36,580
Up to 30% of those who try will completely kick the habit, but most will take multiple attempts.

515
00:38:36,660 --> 00:38:39,660
Success rates double with counseling and medication.

516
00:38:39,661 --> 00:38:45,660
Most ex-smokers say that quitting smoking is the hardest thing that they have ever done in their lives.

517
00:38:45,661 --> 00:38:49,660
Smokers who do quit still have a higher risk of cancer than non-smokers,

518
00:38:49,661 --> 00:38:51,660
but far lower than smokers who don't stop.

519
00:38:51,661 --> 00:38:54,660
There are many lasting health benefits to quitting.

520
00:38:54,661 --> 00:38:56,660
Your general health will improve.

521
00:38:56,661 --> 00:39:00,660
So those people who have emphysema, they'll have less problems.

522
00:39:00,661 --> 00:39:04,660
Those people who have chronic bronchitis will have less acute infections and so on.

523
00:39:04,661 --> 00:39:09,220
quality of life will improve so nobody ever should think I've done it my whole

524
00:39:09,221 --> 00:39:13,240
life I shouldn't stop now many people have little reason to believe that our

525
00:39:13,241 --> 00:39:19,540
society will wean itself from tobacco I think people are going to use tobacco as

526
00:39:19,541 --> 00:39:24,880
long as they can afford it I think the music back a grown right on and on but

527
00:39:24,881 --> 00:39:29,380
the volume may change it may decrease but I still think the back is here to

528
00:39:29,381 --> 00:39:30,380
day.

529
00:39:30,381 --> 00:39:34,580
Will we see this product gone in 20 to 30 years?

530
00:39:34,581 --> 00:39:36,720
I don't think so.

531
00:39:36,721 --> 00:39:40,500
Do I think it's going to become more regulated and constrained?

532
00:39:40,501 --> 00:39:43,260
Yes, it's happening.

533
00:39:43,261 --> 00:39:47,680
Regulated or not, tobacco has been with humankind for thousands of years.

534
00:39:47,681 --> 00:39:52,400
And increasingly, this contradictory crop that generates profits and has become a source

535
00:39:52,401 --> 00:39:58,620
of bitter conflict will continue to pit pleasure against mortality.

